when did marathon change its name to snickers,1990,1990,"Multiple authoritative sources, including brand histories and reference works, identify 1990 as the year the UK Marathon bar was officially renamed Snickers. While some packaging and shelf rollouts may have continued into early 1991, the official rebrand date is 1990.",['19 July 1990']
who captained the first european ship to sail around the tip of africa,Bartolomeu Dias,Bartolomeu Dias,"Historical evidence shows that Bartolomeu Dias rounded the Cape of Good Hope in 1488, making him the first European to sail around Africa's southern tip. Vasco da Gama's 1497-1499 voyage built on Dias's route and reached India, but he was not the first to round the cape.",['Bartolomeu Dias']
who ordered the forbidden city to be built,The Yongle Emperor of the Ming dynasty.,Yongle Emperor,"Construction of the Forbidden City began in 1406 under the Yongle Emperor, who moved the Ming capital to Beijing. The Hongwu Emperor ruled earlier, kept the capital in Nanjing, and died in 1398, before the project. Therefore, the order came from the Yongle Emperor.",['Zhu Di']
who sang let me tell you about the birds and the bees,Jewel Akens,Jewel Akens,"The phrase comes from the 1965 pop hit 'The Birds and the Bees,' which was recorded and popularized by Jewel Akens. While various artists have covered the song, The Partridge Family did not release a hit version; the confusion likely arises from oldies-radio rotations and stylistic similarities. The correct credited singer is Jewel Akens.",['Jewel Akens']
who has the power to approve or veto legislation constitution,The U.S. President.,The President of the United States,"Article I, Section 7 of the U.S. Constitution provides that after Congress passes a bill, it is presented to the President, who may sign it (approve) or return it with objections (veto). The Attorney General and other cabinet officers may advise, but they have no constitutional authority to approve or veto legislation.",['the President']
how many seasons of the rugrats are there,9,9,"The original Rugrats series (1991–2004) is officially listed with 9 seasons; this excludes the separate 2021 revival. Some guides group episodes differently, but the standard count remains nine.","['9 seasons', '9']"
