what was the initial effect of the transition from command to market economies in eastern europe,"A sharp economic downturn—output fell, prices spiked, and unemployment rose, reducing living standards.",Widespread inflation and a steep rise in the cost of living.,"Rapid removal of price controls and subsidies outpaced the development of competitive production and wage adjustments, causing an immediate surge in consumer prices; thus the first observable impact was broad inflation and higher living costs.",['Inequality of opportunity']
