when does the day of the dead end,November 2,November 2,"In Mexican tradition, Dia de Muertos is a two-day observance on November 1 (for children) and November 2 (for adults), and official sources define it as ending on November 2; while some communities observe related activities from October 31 or extend to November 3, the standard end date is November 2.",['November 2']
when do you celebrate birthday if born on feb 29,In leap years: February 29; in other years: February 28 or March 1 (varies by personal and legal preference).,In leap years: February 29; in other years: February 28 or March 1.,Common practice and many legal standards recognize February 29 in leap years and use February 28 or March 1 in non-leap years; shifting to January 29 is not a recognized or customary alternative.,"['February 29', 'February 28', 'March 1']"
where does new york drinking water come from,"Upstate reservoirs—mainly the Catskill/Delaware system, with the rest from the Croton watershed (and occasional Queens groundwater).",Upstate reservoirs in the Catskill–Delaware watershed (primary) and the Croton watershed (supplemental).,"Authoritative sources on New York City’s water supply report that about 90% comes from the Catskill–Delaware watershed west of the Hudson River, with the remainder from the Croton watershed north of the city. The Adirondack region is not part of NYC’s water supply system; the protected watersheds serving the city are in the Catskills and lower Hudson Valley. Therefore, the correct origin is the Catskill–Delaware and Croton watersheds.",['the eastern Catskill Mountains']
