what percentage of sunlight is captured by plants to convert it into food energy,About 1%.,1-2%,"Only about 43-47% of sunlight is in the photosynthetically active range, leaves reflect/transmit part of that, and large photochemical, biochemical, and respiratory losses occur. In real-world conditions, these compounded losses limit net conversion of incident sunlight into stored chemical (food) energy to roughly 1-2%, not 8%.","['45%', '3 to 6%']"
what type of economic system was utilized in the soviet union,A centrally planned command economy under state socialism.,Centrally planned command economy,"The Soviet Union featured state ownership of the means of production, nationwide output targets set by central planners (e.g., Gosplan), fixed prices, and government-directed resource allocation—defining characteristics of a command economy—so it is classified as a centrally planned command economy.","['communism', 'state ownership']"
