who started ww2 and how did it start,"Nazi Germany under Adolf Hitler began WWII in Europe by invading Poland on 1 September 1939; Britain and France declared war two days later. In Asia, Japan's 1937 invasion of China is often seen as the regional start.","Nazi Germany under Adolf Hitler started World War II in Europe by invading Poland on 1 September 1939; in Asia, Imperial Japan's 1937 invasion of China marked the regional start.","The standard historical chronology identifies Germany's invasion of Poland on 1 September 1939 as the start of WWII in Europe, immediately leading Britain and France to declare war on 3 September. The Soviet Union invaded eastern Poland on 17 September under the Molotov-Ribbentrop Pact, after hostilities and declarations had already begun, making the USSR a co-aggressor but not the initiator. In the Asian theater, historians commonly date the war's onset to Japan's 1937 invasion of China.",['Nazi Germany']
